# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the PLATFORMZ server (E3).
#
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=$PWD/server/test/tsan.supp" \
#   PLATFORMZ_SERVER_BIN=gameserver-tsan ./server/test/run_probes.sh
#
# KEEP THIS FILE SHORT. Every line here is a class of bug the job can no longer
# find, so each one needs a reason that is about the standard or the runtime -
# never "this one was noisy" or "we think it is fine".

# std::cout, written from the sim thread and from the io threads.
#
# [iostream.objects] is explicit that concurrent formatted output to a
# synchronized standard stream "shall not result in a data race" - the characters
# may interleave, but the object itself is safe. libc++ and libstdc++ implement
# that without annotating it for TSan, so TSan sees two threads touching the
# stream's internal state and reports the implementation, not our code.
#
# This is the only report the whole probe suite produced, and leaving it in would
# bury the next real one under it - which is the actual cost of an unsuppressed
# false positive.
#
# The cosmetic half IS real: two log lines can interleave in journalctl. If that
# ever stops being cosmetic, the fix is one mutex-guarded Log() helper in
# server_main.cpp, not deleting these lines.
race:__pad_and_output
race:__put_character_sequence
race:std::__1::basic_ostream
race:std::basic_ostream
